{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And with the choicest of the earth and its fullness</b> — the choicest of the flatland, and that with which it is filled. For he mentioned the mountains and the hills, and he will mention the valley and the land of the plain, according to the words of Rabbi Abraham (Ibn Ezra on Deuteronomy 33:16). But in my opinion, 'the choicest of the land and its fullness' corresponds to 'blessings of the breasts and womb,' for all people and all creeping things that have life are called 'its fullness,' and likewise 'let the sea roar and its fullness' (Psalms 96:11), 'for I will fill you with people, like the locust' (Jeremiah 51:14). And behold, this is like the sense of 'blessed be the fruit of your womb and the fruit of your land and the fruit of your cattle' (Deuteronomy 28:4)." "'And the favor of Him who dwelt in the bush' is drawn from above — 'and from the favor of Him who dwelt in the bush.' And the honored Name is called <b>Him who dwelt in the bush</b>, because there He first appeared to him, and He dwelt for many days upon Mount Sinai, which is the place of the bush, and from Sinai He came and dwelt in Israel. And the sense of the verse is that his land will be blessed through the favor of the Name, in the sense of 'You, O YHWH, favored Your land' (Psalms 85:2), and 'I will favor it and I will be glorified' (Haggai 1:8)." "And the sense of <b>let it come</b> is: this blessing shall come upon the head of Joseph and upon the crown of the prince among his brothers. Or its sense is: the favor of Him who dwelt in the bush shall come upon the head of Joseph. And do not wonder at the word חֵפֶץ (favor) that He feminizes it, for so in the Aramaic tongue: 'and the king's favor' (Ezra 5:17), and in the language of the Sages: חֶפְצַת נַפְשׁוֹ (the desire of his soul). And by way of truth, one may say that the רָצוֹן (favor) that dwelt in the bush — it shall come upon the head of Joseph; through it he shall lift up his head. And he placed the word in construct proximity in a place of recognition [מֻכְרָת], and there are many like it. Or it may be attached to the honored Name mentioned above: 'and the favor of YHWH who dwells in the bush shall come upon the head of Joseph.' And this is the blessing of Jacob (Genesis 49:25): 'from the El of your father and He will help you, and from Shaddai and He will bless you.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T02:59:33.111421274Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}